course: dictionary
lesson: 12371
title: The crossword puzzle
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A crossword is a word puzzle. It is a grid of white squares, and you write words into the squares. Each word is found by reading a clue. «Grandad does the crossword every morning with his tea.»
explain: The words go across, from left to right, and down, from top to bottom. Each answer must fit the squares it sits in. «Where the two words cross, they share one square, so the letter must be the same in both.»
explain: Crosswords are good for learning. At school they help you practise spelling and new vocabulary. A clue such as «a large animal with a long trunk» gives you a word to find, and the letters you have already written help you check it.
fact: A crossword is a word puzzle made of a grid of squares.
fact: The words in a crossword go across and down.
fact: Each word is found by reading a clue.
fact: Where two words cross, they share one square, so the letter must match.
fact: In maths, number crosswords use sums as clues.
exercise: What is a crossword? | *A word puzzle where you write words into a grid of squares | A race around a sports field | A kind of sandwich | A long story about a river crossing
exercise: Which way do the words in a crossword go? | *Across and down | Round in a circle | Up the stairs | Backwards only
exercise: In a crossword, what helps you find each word? | Pictures of animals | *A clue | A map of the town | The number of pages in a book
test: «Mia wrote the answer to 3 across, then checked it against 2 down.» Why did she check? | *Where the words cross, the letters must match | To find the clue for 3 across | To make the grid bigger | Crosswords have no rules
test: In a number crossword, what do the clues use? | Colours | Pictures of animals | Songs | *Sums
exam: «Ben did the crossword at school to practise his spelling.» What does crossword mean here? | A long walk to school | *A word puzzle in a grid of squares | A type of school bus | A road where two streets meet
